// Port Royal and the approaches to Kingston Harbour, Jamaica, c. 1715.
//
// Coordinates are (latitude, longitude) in degrees, eyeballed from modern
// geography as a first pass. Refine against real coastline data later.
// Historical notes:
//   - Port Royal sits on the western tip of the Palisadoes, a long sand spit
//     enclosing Kingston Harbour. The 1692 earthquake sank much of the town,
//     and a fire in 1703 burned most of the rest. By 1715 it is a smaller
//     town and the Royal Navy's base in the Caribbean.
//   - Kingston, founded in 1692 on the harbour's north shore, is growing into
//     the island's commercial port.
//   - The Port Royal Cays lie off the point. Rackham's Cay is named for
//     "Calico Jack" Rackham, whose body was gibbeted there in 1720.
(
    name: "Port Royal",
    origin: (17.9372, -76.8435),
    // Geography is drawn at half real size so passages take minutes, not hours.
    // Ships stay true scale. See the creative-license log in docs/DESIGN.md.
    distance_scale: 0.5,
    // South of the cays, running west before the trade wind toward the point.
    player_start: (
        position: (17.9050, -76.7900),
        heading_degrees: 270.0,
    ),
    land: [
        (
            name: "Jamaica",
            terrain: Forest,
            label: Some((17.9900, -76.8200)),
            outline: [
                // South coast, west to east: Hellshire, Port Henderson,
                // the harbour's north shore past Kingston, then east of the harbour.
